  "reason": "The current best (config_019, acc=0.5251) uses multimodal + multiprofile + scgpt + resnet50 + avgpool + weighted. The singleprofile experiments showed imagenet_vit_l was marginally better than resnet50 (0.4224 vs 0.4214), but the difference was small when only one image embedding was used. With multiprofile avgpool, multiple image embeddings are averaged, so a richer per-profile image representation (ViT-L) could provide more discriminative features to aggregate, potentially yielding a larger gain. config_037 is a clean one-variable change (resnet50→imagenet_vit_l) from the best config, keeping the proven avgpool aggregation and weighted fusion. This is the highest-value exploitation step: if it improves, we lock in a stronger baseline for the remaining 3 experiments to further refine (e.g., testing concat fusion or scvi_n200); if it doesn't, we confirm resnet50 is sufficient and can pivot to other axes."
